# Nura motion system (must follow)

The brand lives through motion. Everything animates from one set of tokens, so
new sections stay consistent instead of drifting. **Extend the shared component,
never invent a one-off tween.**

Source of truth:
- Tokens + presets: `lib/motion.ts` (mirrored as `--mo-*` in
  `app/components/motion/motion.css`)
- Page transitions: `lib/page-transitions.ts` + `app/components/motion/page-transitions.css`
- Components: `app/components/motion/` (`Reveal`, `StaggerText`, `CountUp`,
  `Marquee`, `SectionRise`, `SectionWipe`, `SectionBloom`,
  `PageTransitionOverlay`, `MotionProvider`)

## Tokens (never hardcode)

- Duration: `--mo-dur-instant/fast/base/slow/slower` (.18 → 1.35s)
- Easing: `--mo-ease-out` (arrivals), `--mo-ease-in-out` (transitions),
  `--mo-ease-soft` (hovers), `--mo-ease-wave` (the brand lift), `--mo-ease-pop`
- Stagger: `--mo-stagger` (.045s)
- Shadows: `--mo-shadow-lift`, `--mo-shadow-card` (ink-tinted, never neutral black)

The legacy `--ease` var and the existing GSAP `.fe-animate` / letter-rise
entrances stay; new work uses the motion primitives.

## What to use where

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Content entrance on scroll | `Reveal` |
| Lead paragraph / mid-weight heading rise | `StaggerText` |
| Big marketing section H2 | `LetterRevealHeading` (letter-rise — see `letter-rise-headings.mdc`) |
| Number counting up | `CountUp` |
| Horizontal ticker | `Marquee` |
| Section opens from an inset card as it scrolls in | `SectionRise` |
| Next section wiped in by a wave-edged veil | `SectionWipe` |
| Next section eased in by a pistachio bloom | `SectionBloom` (available, not wired) |
| Route change | `PageTransitionOverlay` (mounted once in `FrontendShellClient`) |
| Card hover / press feedback | `interactions.css` utilities (`.mo-lift`, `.mo-press`, `.mo-underline`) |

## Hard rules

1. **Reduced motion.** Every pattern collapses to plain stacked blocks: no clip,
   no pin, no transform. Both `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` and the
   site-wide `html[data-a11y-motion="reduced"]` attribute must be handled, and
   content that starts hidden must be forced visible.
2. **No reuse on neighbours.** Two adjacent section hand-offs must differ. Check
   the current order in `HomeLanding.tsx` before adding one; add any new pattern
   to the catalogue in `docs/motion-brand.md`.
3. **No invisible click blockers.** Any full-size overlay is `pointer-events: none`;
   only the visible panel inside it is `pointer-events: auto`. (The page-transition
   overlay is `auto` only during the cover phase.)
4. **No layout shift.** Scroll hand-offs use `clip-path` / `transform` / `opacity`
   only — never negative margins, spacers or pins that leave gaps.
5. **Scroll-linked effects are linear in scroll.** Easing belongs to time-based
   animations only. Never tie a tween to scroll position with a time-based ease.
6. **Don't clip sticky sections.** `SectionRise` / `SectionWipe` / `SectionBloom`
   (clip / overflow) must not wrap a section with `position: sticky` / `fixed`
   children — clipping creates a containing block and breaks them. This is why
   `SessionPathSticky` ("how it works") stays plain.
7. **SSR must match.** Start states are deterministic (inline style vars from
   props), never read `window` during render.
8. **Palette only.** Transitions and overlays use the pistachio palette (mint,
   pistachio, sage, olive-ink, ink, ground/white). No new colours.

## Page transitions

One transition is active site-wide; default `waveSweep`. Do not add a second
overlay or per-page transition. New transitions go in `PAGE_TRANSITIONS` +
`transitionLayers` (`lib/page-transitions.ts`) and a matching `[data-pt="…"]`
block in `page-transitions.css`. The shop/app flows may run a notch faster
(`FAST_FACTOR`).
